{"additions":56,"author":{"id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","is_bot":false,"login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"},"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"b176747b339685e781de04268c46b7ae123abfbf","changedFiles":3,"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-10T23:35:54Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"hu3mann"},{"email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","id":"BOT_kgDOCZ5PDw","login":"google-labs-jules[bot]","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-10T23:35:54Z","messageBody":"This change implements a two-step confirmation pattern for the \"Skip\" action in the TaskSequencer component. Users now need to click the Skip button twice within a 3-second window to confirm a skip, preventing impulsive or accidental sequence jumps.\n\nKey improvements:\n- Added `isSkipConfirming` state with a 3-second auto-reset.\n- Swapped Skip icon to `AlertTriangle` and updated label to \"Confirm Skip?\" during the pending state.\n- Added `skip-pulse` animation for visual reinforcement during confirmation.\n- Updated `aria-label` to be context-aware (Confirm skip vs Skip to [Task]).\n- Fixed a pre-existing ARIA role violation in `PredictionPanel.tsx` tests during loading state.\n- Verified with accessibility tests and manual frontend verification.\n\n♿ Accessibility: Ensures non-reversible sequence jumps have clear confirmation and descriptive ARIA labels.\n\nCo-authored-by: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(ui): add soft confirmation for skip task action","oid":"283d6667933f2fd161992088731b7a6f8024f001"}],"createdAt":"2026-07-10T23:35:58Z","deletions":11,"headRefName":"palette-task-skip-soft-confirm-774176508838366537","headRefOid":"283d6667933f2fd161992088731b7a6f8024f001","isDraft":false,"labels":[],"mergeCommit":null,"mergedAt":null,"number":1038,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDOPyIw988AAAABFrBBqg","author":{